- e_Plx (error in parallax): High error reduces reliability of distance and absolute magnitude estimation, affecting giant classification confidence.  
- B-V (color index): Giants often have larger B-V (redder colors) than dwarfs of the same spectral type, but color alone is not definitive.  
- SpType (spectral type): Luminosity class in SpType is crucial; giants have "III" or intermediate classes like "III/IV" or "Ib/II", dwarfs have "V".  
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Giants have lower absolute magnitude (brighter) than dwarfs; thus, smaller Amag values correlate with giants.

