Class 0 (not giant) stars generally have dwarf spectral types (V), higher Amag (fainter absolute magnitude), smaller B-V, and larger parallaxes.  
Class 1 (giant) stars have spectral types with luminosity class III or higher, lower Amag (brighter absolute magnitude), larger B-V, and smaller parallaxes.

