- e_Plx (error in parallax): High error reduces reliability of distance estimates; less useful directly for classification.
- B-V (color index): Color index correlates with temperature and spectral type; giants often have certain color ranges but overlap exists.
- SpType (spectral type): The luminosity class (V = dwarf/main sequence, III = giant, Ib/II = bright giant/supergiant) is the most direct indicator of giant status.
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Giants are intrinsically brighter, so Amag is numerically smaller (brighter) than dwarfs; higher Amag (fainter) stars tend to be dwarfs.

